{
  "id": "Compound::DB08906 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Fluticasone Furoate, a fluorinated steroid, is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Fluticasone Furoate may act as a substrate for Cyp3a4, as it is linked to the induction of Cyp3a4 through the activation of glucocorticoid receptors. This is supported by the fact that both Fluticasone Furoate and Fluorometholone, which are related to it, bind to Cyp3a4, indicating a potential mechanism of enzyme induction. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Cyp3a4, including the involvement of therapeutic glucocorticoids, suggests a broader role of Fluticasone Furoate in modulating Cyp3a4 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of glucocorticoid receptor signaling in the regulation of Cyp3a4, with Fluticasone Furoate potentially serving as a key mediator in this process.",
